---
// "Why xdelta3 works on ZIP files" — credibility paragraph per v5 §4.1.
// The 61,400%-smaller single-file result is the proof.
---

<section class="mechanism fade-up delay-1">
  <span class="section-eyebrow">The mechanism</span>
  <h2>It works on already-compressed archives</h2>

  <div class="mechanism-stat">
    <div class="stat-number">61,400%</div>
    <div class="stat-label">
      smaller on compressed input — a 91 MB ZIP (a real ReadonlyREST
      plugin) stored as a 148 KB diff against the previous release.
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Release after release, a ZIP or JAR contains the same entries in the
    same order — same <code>manifest.mf</code>, same icons, same bundled
    CSS. The bytes repeat, so the binary diff between two releases stays
    tiny even though each file is internally compressed.
  </p>

  <p>
    → <a href="/docs/explanation/delta-compression">Read the engineering note</a>
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .mechanism-stat {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 12px;
    max-width: var(--measure-wide);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .mechanism-stat:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 15px 35px -10px rgba(25, 230, 203, 0.15);
    border-color: var(--brand-soft);
  }

  .stat-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--brand);
    line-height: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(25, 230, 203, 0.3);
  }

  .stat-label {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .mechanism-stat {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
